{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"32a93d593c1992b556b3bac42ba9921cccbf1fee"},"timestamp":1511200076,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzU0NDI2NTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1974","origin":"github"},"title":"Datalad adds to annex files that were already in git","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nWhenever a file (which was under git) gets modified in a subdataset, and gets added to the parent dataset with `datalad add -d . subdataset`, the file gets committed to annex instead of git.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n\n```terminal\ncontematto@talete /tmp $ datalad create test_dataset\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test_dataset\ncreate(ok): /tmp/test_dataset (dataset)\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp $ cd test_dataset\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ datalad create subdataset\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset\ncreate(ok): /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (dataset)\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master*) $ datalad add -d . subdataset\nadd(ok): subdataset (dataset) [added new subdataset]\nadd(notneeded): subdataset (dataset) [nothing to add from /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset]\nadd(notneeded): .gitmodules (file) [already included in the dataset]\nsave(ok): /tmp/test_dataset (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 2, ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ cd subdataset\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (master) $ touch myfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (master*) $ git add myfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (master*) $ git commit -m \"Added file\"\n[master 1c48f6d] Added file\n 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 myfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (master) $ ls\nmyfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (master) $ cd ..\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master*) $ ls\nsubdataset\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master*) $ datalad add -d . subdataset\nadd(notneeded): subdataset/myfileingit.txt (file) [already included in the dataset]\nadd(notneeded): subdataset (dataset) [already known subdataset]\nsave(notneeded): /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (dataset)\nsave(ok): /tmp/test_dataset (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 2)\n  save (notneeded: 1, ok: 1)\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ ls -l subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n-rw-r--r--  1 contematto  wheel  0 Nov 20 12:42 subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ echo \"adding stuff\" \u003e\u003e subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ datalad add -d . subdataset\nadd(ok): subdataset/myfileingit.txt (file)\nadd(notneeded): subdataset (dataset) [already known subdataset]\nsave(ok): /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (dataset)\nsave(ok): /tmp/test_dataset (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (notneeded: 1, ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 2)\n\ncontematto@talete /tmp/test_dataset (master) $ ls -l subdataset\ntotal 8\nlrwxr-xr-x  1 contematto  wheel  118 Nov 20 12:43 myfileingit.txt -\u003e .git/annex/objects/x4/xK/MD5E-s13--ef8174b2381e2ac9c2b0f2a8a39e5031.txt/MD5E-s13--ef8174b2381e2ac9c2b0f2a8a39e5031.txt\n```\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad plugin wtf`)?\n\ndatalad 0.9.1\n\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)\n\nI love datalad \u003c3","files":null}]}